# Luminary marker — cli#460
- date: 2026-11-02
- branch: feat/460-init-brand-mark
- lead: michael-feathers
- supporting: [tony-hoare, donald-norman]
- lead-lens: characterization. The glyph grid is data that an editor paste or a
  font substitution can silently corrupt. The test pins the exact codepoint set
  and row count so corruption fails loudly instead of shipping a broken mark.
- hoare: renderBrandMark is pure. Precondition is a version string and an
  optional width. Postcondition is either the full mark or text-only, never a
  wrapped grid. Width comes in as an argument so the contract is testable
  without a TTY.
- norman: a wrapped mark reads as corruption, not as a narrow terminal. Dropping
  it below 53 columns is the honest signifier.
